t the same input always gives the same answer. Edges into "},{"code":"root","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and self-loops are never weighed; every other edge is weighed once. "},{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not kept."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The algorithm is Chu–Liu\/Edmonds with Tarjan’s contraction over mergeable heaps (skew heaps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with lazy offsets) and a union–find with rollback to expand the contracted cycles.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Negative and zero weights are ordinary weights.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(m log m)."}]}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"root","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a vertex; every weight is finite (not NaN or infinite); the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"differences between weights do not overflow.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"references":{"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/minimumSpanningArborescence(from:weight:)":{"title":"minimumSpanningArborescence(from:weight:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumSpanningArborescence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"from"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},